# #5841, a5e2e2ef's third case: a duplicate claims after the split's row read and before
# its write. A conditional write re-reads and supersedes it; an unconditional one leaves
# the row at the duplicate's own epoch.
MODULE: HandOffBoundSplitRowWriteLosesToClaim
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the split's row write is unconditional, so a duplicate's claim between its read and its write is silently overwritten at the same epoch
PERTURBS: SplitRowWrite
BOUNDS: WithStaleDonor = TRUE, WithPreArm = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ IF eRow = bRead
       THEN /\ eRow' = IF SplitBumps(bRead) THEN bRead + 1 ELSE bRead
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row write does not check the value it read.
    /\ IF TRUE
       THEN /\ eRow' = IF SplitBumps(bRead) THEN bRead + 1 ELSE bRead
--- END
